       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Nothing in the details you gave (normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify going above that. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI bleeding.\n\nWas this a typo? Here are some options:\n- **Usual dosing:** Start at 50 mg once daily. For depression, you can titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least 1 week, up to 200 mg/day. For OCD, PTSD, or panic disorder, the starting dose is often 25 mg.\n- **Already on sertraline:** If this patient is already on a high dose, tell me the current dose. I can then enter the right continuation or titration dose.\n- **Intentional dose above 200 mg:** If it is deliberate, for example a specialist-directed plan, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy or psychiatry first.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
